If PuTTY is connected, you'll see hello host appear instantly. This confirms the pipe is fully working before you commit to the bcdedit/grub changes.

If guest is Windows, open PowerShell in the guest and run:
powershell

$port = New-Object System.IO.Ports.SerialPort "COM1",115200
$port.Open()
$port.WriteLine("hello host")
$port.Close()

What You Should See Once Working

On VM boot you'll get something like:

SeaBIOS (version...)
Booting from Hard Disk...
